From 214b6311fb24438aaefc64e7b2516fcfa212583f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:10:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] poly: keep tessellator state in registers

The CL tessellator generates each patch on one thread. Its per-edge
arrays (tess factor contexts, point counts, odd flags) are indexed by
the ring-loop edge counter, so NIR puts them in scratch, and the inlined
helpers' early returns leave stale return-value phis that are carried
around the ring loops. On Valhall the WITH_COUNTS kernels spilled
1.8-2.1 KiB per thread to TLS (quad: 340 spills, 1367 fills).

Recompute the per-edge values from scalars inside the loop, read the
remaining small arrays through selects (TESS_SEL2/3/4), pack the odd
flags into one bitmask, give PatchIndexValue, PlacePointIn1D and
finalPointPositionTable a single exit, and reset the index-patch context
at the end of each edge so no stale values stay live across the loops.

v9 rel9 compiler: tri WITH_COUNTS tls 1824 -> 0 B (no spills), quad
WITH_COUNTS tls 2112 -> 64 B (9 spills, 385 fills), quad COUNT 1312 -> 0.
Output is unchanged (tess_perf readback hashes match).

tess_perf us/draw, no GS, L=16: TB336FU (v9) 2918 -> 1664,
X6 Pro (v11) 2362 -> 1208.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
